16 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents five boxplots comparing behavioral or clinical metrics \(Speech/Language, Sociability, Sensory/Cognitive, Gastrointestinal, Sleep\) across timepoints T0, T14, and T22, with significance levels indicated. Panel B shows four heatmaps of frequency \(Hertz\) versus time \(milliseconds\) for groups TD and ASD at three timepoints, with a color bar for intensity. Panel C displays a boxplot comparing 40 Hz ITPC between ASD and TD groups, labeled \215ns\216 for not significant. Panel D provides a boxplot comparing 40 Hz ITPC for ASD at T0, T14, and T22, also marked not significant.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a line graph comparing amplitude over time for ASD and TD groups. Panel B displays two scalp topography maps for ASD and TD, with color scales indicating amplitude distribution. Panel C presents a boxplot comparing amplitude between ASD and TD, with a significant difference marked. Panel D shows a line graph of amplitude over time for T0, T14, and T22. Panel E includes three scalp topography maps for T0, T14, and T22. Panel F features a boxplot comparing amplitude across T0, T14, and T22, with statistical significance and non-significance indicated. Panel G contains five scatterplots correlating amplitude with measures such as speech-language communication, sociability, sensory awareness, gastrointestinal symptoms, and sleep, showing trend lines and statistics. Panel H presents five scatterplots correlating amplitude change with changes in the same measures, with trend lines and statistics included.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
